--- !u!114 &1531070632
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 1531070630}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 3269ab77e5738674b9fefab358f453ff, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::UIAnimLab.Station
  Code: I4
  Title: What + gives you
  Summary: Unity fills a new list entry with zeros. The tool patches what's still
    zero, and never what you set.
  Watch: Fresh Player
  WatchObjects:
  - {fileID: 1267473592}
  HowTo: Select Fresh Player. Press + on Animations. Then + on its Steps twice. Change
    the second step's Duration to 0, click elsewhere. Set Loops to 0. Undo everything
    afterwards.
  Expect: The new animation is named New Animation, Loops 1, Apply From Values Immediately
    ticked, Interrupt Others ticked with COMPLETE and REPORT. The first step has
    Duration 0.25 and Out Quad; the second is a copy of the first. Duration 0 becomes
    0.25 again; Loops 0 becomes 1.
